# MediterraneApp

Canonical guidance: [`../../AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Read it first; this rule is a
short pointer.

MediterraneApp is a Spring Boot 4.1 / Java 25 (LTS) REST API for recipes, backed by
PostgreSQL. It is a legacy portfolio project: it builds and has a test suite plus CI,
but no authentication. No database credentials are checked in; supply
`SPRING_DATASOURCE_*` at runtime.

- Run `./mvnw -B verify` before reporting success; it compiles, runs the H2-backed
  test suite, and packages the JAR. CI runs the same command.
- The only controller is `RecipeController` at `/recipe`. There is no ingredient
  endpoint.
- `POST /recipe` upserts by `name` and returns `201` on create, `200` on update.
  `PUT /recipe/{uuid}` treats the path UUID as authoritative; an optional body UUID must
  match or the request returns `400` and leaves the row unchanged.
- Never add credentials to `src/main/resources/application.yml` or copy them into code,
  docs, commits, or chat. See [`../../SECURITY.md`](../../SECURITY.md).
- Keep Java 25 (LTS), Spring Boot 4.1, the hand-written mappers, and the current API
  shape unless a migration or breaking change is explicitly requested.
- Update [`../../docs/API.md`](../../docs/API.md) and
  [`../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) when behavior changes.

For work in another repository, read that repository's own `AGENTS.md` first.
